# Normalize all text files to LF, regardless of the checkout platform's
# core.autocrlf setting. Without this, npm's lockfile writer on Windows can
# emit package-lock.json with CRLF line endings while every other file in
# this repo (edited via LF-default tooling, or normalized by `npm run
# format`, whose Prettier config defaults to endOfLine: "lf") stays LF --
# the resulting mismatch is exactly what caused `npm run format:check` to
# flag package-lock.json even though its actual JSON content was correctly
# formatted. This file makes the LF convention explicit and durable instead
# of relying on each contributor's local git/OS configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf
